# Commands that use a store config/remote-local-paths keeps on the remote's own disk, so
# they run on dev under every --where (the remote-local rule). Container tools keep their
# images and containers under ~/.local/share/containers and ~/.cache/containers: offloaded,
# a build's image would stay on the remote. A cache command would clean the remote's copy
# and leave dev's as it was. Entries are read as config/local-only's are.
podman
podman-compose
buildah
skopeo
docker
docker-compose
go clean
uv cache
pre-commit clean
pre-commit gc
pre_commit clean
pre_commit gc
